0050:     - Bend pixels whose turn direction is the majority direction for that cycle are convex corners and become yellow.
0051:     - Bend pixels whose turn direction is the minority direction for that cycle are concave corners and become red.
0052:     Key insight
0053:     - A simple rectilinear closed boundary has exactly four more convex bends than concave bends, so convexity can be inferred structurally from the majority turn sign within each traced cycle.
0054:     """
